export anchor BroadsheetStyle:
    number: 78
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Broadsheet
    idea: The dashboard is a dense daily front page where the most urgent fact is the banner headline, each project is a story with a dateline and a jump line, and the numbers live in a ruled sidebar.
    base: light
    palette:
        newsprint: #f3f0e6, the page sheet
        table: #e3dfd3, the surround behind the sheet
        ink: #191919, text, rules and solid bars
        grey: #545454, bylines, cutlines and jump lines
        hairline: #b7b2a5, column rules and dotted list rules
        halftone: #e6e1d2, hatched photo boxes
        red: #9b1b1b, the kicker, wire times and Behind
        green: #2b5a2d, the On track tag
        brown: #774a00, the At risk tag
        highlighter: #fff6c9, the focus fill
    type:
        Four stacks. The nameplate uses Old English Text MT, Goudy Text MT,
        Times New Roman at 76px. Headlines use Times New Roman, Times,
        Liberation Serif at 700, the banner 54px, the lead story 34px,
        second stories 22px and briefs 18px. Decks are 20px italic. Body is
        Georgia 14px at 1.42, justified with hyphens in columns. Labels,
        datelines and tags use Franklin Gothic, Arial Narrow, Arial at 11px
        bold caps.
    layout:
        A utility strip has an underlined search, Notices (3), Mara Okafor
        and a black New project button. The nameplate row has a boxed ear on
        each side, This week 73 done and Outlook 4 overdue, around the big
        Brightwork. A folio line under a 3px rule gives the date, the team
        edition for Mara Okafor and Six projects inside. Nav is a centred
        section index with Home inverted. The banner has the red kicker Good
        morning, Mara, the headline Four Tasks Overdue as Billing Migration
        Falls Behind and an italic deck. The front splits into a main area
        and a rail divided by a 1px ink rule. The lead story is Billing
        migration with a figures line, a drop cap and three justified
        columns with rules, ending in a jump line. Under it Mobile app 2.0
        runs in two columns beside Website redesign with a hatched photo
        box showing 72 percent and a cutline, then three briefs. The rail
        has a boxed By the numbers list, a Fig. 1 bar chart with open bars
        last week and solid bars this week, and an In brief wire. At 375px
        everything is one column.
    spacing: Tight. 14px between stories and 18px gutters with a rule in each.
    density: Very high. Three text columns in the lead and briefs in threes.
    corners: None.
    borders: A 3px rule under the nameplate, 1px ink between main and rail, hairline column rules, 2px boxes in the rail and dotted list rules.
    shadows: None on the page. The sheet sits on a darker table.
    icons:
        No pictograms. Printer’s shapes before status tags, a disc for On
        track, a triangle for At risk and a square for Behind. Each story
        also has a small ruled progress bar.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 2px over a pale yellow highlighter fill.
    tone: Headline English, such as Four Tasks Overdue as Billing Migration Falls Behind, desk datelines and Continued in.
